Title: 0010-sdl2-keysym-to-ansi-no-character
Repository: grafx2
Base-Commit: f84cb09dc59d706d6e7b28778b01ba911f52298c
Requires: 0009-aros-absolute-parent-directory.patch
Author: aros-grafx2 project
Date: 2026-09-22
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: Generic SDL2 code in src/keyboard.c; affects readline and file-selector quicksearch on every SDL2 build. Upstream candidate.

Problem:
  In a text field on AROS, Shift, Ctrl, Alt, Amiga, Caps Lock, the function keys and the keypad operators insert stray characters (Shift gives 0xE1, F1 gives ':', keypad + gives 'W'). The SDL2 Keysym_to_ANSI() returns K2K(sym), a keycode, for every keysym at or above 128, and AROS SDL2 never emits SDL_TEXTINPUT, so the KEYDOWN path from patch 0003 inserts that keycode as a character. The SDL 1.2 version returns 0 for such keys.
Solution:
  For a scancode-based keysym return the keypad character (digits, . - + / * Enter) or 0, as the SDL 1.2 version does; a plain Unicode keycode is returned as itself. Host test tests/test-keysym-to-ansi.py; guest evidence docs/attachments/2026-09-22-keyboard-modifiers/.
Validation:
  Host: python3 tests/test-keysym-to-ansi.py, 10 failures on the old code,
  0 on the new. Guest 2026-09-22, AROS One 1.3 x86_64 ABIv11 under QEMU: F2 Save picture, click Filename, press Shift Ctrl Alt Amiga
  CapsLock CapsLock KP- KP+ - Shift+= F1 F3 then type ok. Before:
  NO_NAME.GIFáàâã99UW-á=:<ok. After: NO_NAME.GIF+-=ok. Comment field
  after: keypad / * + typed, Left then X gave aXb. Report in
  docs/attachments/2026-09-22-keyboard-modifiers/REPORT.md.
Removal:
  Permanent fix; nothing to remove. Known remaining limits: shifted
  punctuation on the main row is not resolved (Shift+= types =), and under
  QEMU AROS One maps the PC keypad operator row one key off (KP- arrives
  as KP*), which is outside GrafX2.

diff --git a/src/keyboard.c b/src/keyboard.c
index 4b79e364..e114d15d 100644
--- a/src/keyboard.c
+++ b/src/keyboard.c
@@ -858,14 +858,30 @@ word Keysym_to_ANSI(SDL_Keysym keysym)
       return (word)(keysym.sym - 32);  // uppercase letter
     else
       return (word)keysym.sym;
-  } else {
-    if (keysym.sym >= SDLK_KP_1 && keysym.sym <= SDLK_KP_9)
-      return (word)(keysym.sym - SDLK_KP_1 + '1');
-    else if (keysym.sym == SDLK_KP_0)
-      return (word)'0';
-    else
-      return K2K(keysym.sym);
   }
+  if (keysym.sym & SDLK_SCANCODE_MASK) {
+    // Keys that have no character of their own. The keypad is the one
+    // group that does; everything else (modifiers, function keys, cursor
+    // keys, ...) is 0, as in the SDL 1.2 version above. Returning the
+    // keycode here made every consumer of Key_ANSI as a character insert
+    // garbage: Shift became 0xE1, F1 became ':', keypad + became 'W'.
+    switch (keysym.sym) {
+      case SDLK_KP_0:        return (word)'0';
+      case SDLK_KP_PERIOD:   return (word)'.';
+      case SDLK_KP_MINUS:    return (word)'-';
+      case SDLK_KP_PLUS:     return (word)'+';
+      case SDLK_KP_DIVIDE:   return (word)'/';
+      case SDLK_KP_MULTIPLY: return (word)'*';
+      case SDLK_KP_ENTER:    return (word)'\r';
+      default:
+        if (keysym.sym >= SDLK_KP_1 && keysym.sym <= SDLK_KP_9)
+          return (word)(keysym.sym - SDLK_KP_1 + '1');
+        return 0;
+    }
+  }
+  // A keycode without the scancode bit is a Unicode code point from the
+  // keymap (accented letters and the like); it is the character.
+  return (word)keysym.sym;
 }
 
 word Key_for_scancode(word scancode)
